1.What is Shift-Left Testing?

Shift-Left Testing means testing activities are moved earlier in the Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC).
Instead of testing only after development, testing starts from the requirement and design phase itself.
Testing starts early and focus on preventing defects
Developers and testers work together
Mostly used in Agile & DevOps

Example:
If you are building a login page:
In Shift-Left, tester reviews requirement:
Should password be minimum 8 characters?
Should it allow special characters?
Issues are found before coding starts.

Advantages:
Early bug detection
Reduced cost of fixing defects
Better product quality
Less rework

Disadvantages:
Requires skilled testers
Requires strong collaboration

->What is Shift-Right Testing?

Shift-Right Testing means testing is performed after the product is released or in the production environment.
It focuses on monitoring real-time user behavior and performance.
Testing after deployment and Focus on user experience
Includes monitoring, performance testing
Used in DevOps & Continuous Delivery

Example:
After releasing a shopping app:
Monitor how many users face payment failure
Check app crashes
Analyze performance during peak time

Advantages:
Real-time feedback
Improves customer experience
Detects production issues

Disadvantages:
Bugs are found late
May affect real users

Difference Between Shift-Left and Shift-Right Testing
   Basis	                            Shift-Left Testing	                               Shift-Right Testing
When Testing Happens            Before coding / Early stages	                            After deployment
Main Focus	                        Defect Prevention	                            User Experience & Monitoring
Environment	                          Development	                                             Production
Cost of Bug Fix	                        Low	                                                      High
Example	                           Requirement review	                               Monitoring app crash reports
